{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/535064-translating-arisen-to-other-cultures","id":535064,"title":"Translating Arisen to Other Cultures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-31T19:34:22-07:00","id":535064,"title":"Translating Arisen to Other Cultures","content":"So, I'm trying to translate the Arisen template to non-Egyptian/Iremite cultures. I'm at the Pillars, and to accurately translate them I'm first breaking them down to their core qualities and representations, as filtered through the Manifestation and Decree write-ups. This has been fairly easy for most of them, but I'm having difficulty with Sheut, as expressed through the Jackal-Headed Decree.<br /> <br /> The Decree implies a certain mystical or spiritual nature to the Sheut (which would be an easy enough concept to translate), but that seems secondary to a sort of nihilism that appears endemic to the Jackal-Headed. So my question, then, is if this nihilism is directly a quality of Sheut, or merely a side-effect of their spirituality being aimed at such a bleak spiritual future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:13:30-07:00","id":535143,"title":"","content":"A little of column A (Sheut is, after all, associated with the &quot;darker&quot; magic, shadows, death, and so on, suggesting a darkness inherent to those who explore it) and a little of column B (being a philosopher in the World of Darkness probably takes you to some pretty dark places, particularly when you're an undying slave bound to Lovecraftian horrors in the underworld), I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T21:38:04-07:00","id":535195,"title":"","content":"Why not just change the values altogether? I've considered Chinese Immortals with the Five Elements before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T22:02:05-07:00","id":535224,"title":"","content":"Well, the first reason that springs to mind is that if you want the &quot;canon&quot; non-Egyptian Mummies, you're generally looking at Twice-Arisen with low Memory or Arisen who have otherwise adopted the cultural trappings of their current home. In that particular case, what each Decree stands for wouldn't change, but the words used to describe them certainly would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:03:33-07:00","id":535911,"title":"","content":"The second reason being that the assumption of certain qualities being the same across the board means having to change very little later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T02:57:46-07:00","id":540812,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Lemme try one with the Five Agents from Taoism<br /> <br /> Sheut - Metal : The shadow-soul is apparently related to death, and something about understanding the Judges I think? The agent of Metal is associated with the direction of West (where the sun sets, and thus connected to death) and the virtue of Justice/Righteousness, something also connected to the 'Judges'.<br /> <br /> Ka - Earth : The essence-soul, revealed in the blog to be related to the Obrimos Path and the subtle Arcanum of Prime, would be at home with the agent of Earth, the base and foundation of creation, aligned with the direction of Center and the virtue of Trust/Faith.<br /> <br /> Ba - Fire : The spirit-soul is the source of will and action. And the agent of Fire has always been associated with actions, be it impulsive or not. The direction of South houses the virtue of Civility/Politeness, which strongly requires action as well (Anyone can know and speak about what's polite, but it takes time and action to really ingrain it to your character)<br /> <br /> Ab - Wood : The heart-soul is the seat of emotions. It's also connected to the Thyrsus Path, and thus the subtle Arcanum of Spirit, and thus the gross Arcanum of Life. Both Spirit and Life grow and feel, which is what Wood is all about. The direction of East leads to the virtue of Compassion/Kindness, which is a virtue about what you feel about others.<br /> <br /> Ren - Water : The name-soul dictates your destiny, something that Northeast Asians also vaguely know about (we have a lot of traditions about names being important for your life). Now, why Water you say? Well, the agent of Water is connected to the virtue of Wisdom, and would not someone who knows about his/her own destiny and that of others be wise? Also, Water is connected to the North... specifically, the star of Polaris; the one star that shines brightest in the heavens. Stars are always associated with fate around the world, especially major ones like Polaris. The Chinese say that the god/saint/immortal of Polaris is the same divinity that dictates the lifespan of people- in other words, their Fate and their Time in this world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}